you  good afternoon from Brussels and welcome  to the live chat with the European  Commissioner for transport  mrs. Adina Berlin Commissioner welcome  to the studio thank you for inviting me  safe travels summer 2020 this is the  title of today's citizens dialogue which  we are doing it we are doing online  after the spring we had everybody wants  to travel now and either for leisure  seeing family reuniting family even we  need to travel safely because as you  said in many occasions until we don't  find a vaccine that is widely available  for coronavirus we have to learn to live  and travel with it we have received a  lot of questions about how travel safe  this summer in Europe not only in Europe  since we started advertising this this  live chat with you  we also gonna take some live questions  as we are obviously live on the Facebook  and Twitter of the European Commission  so as I said a lot of questions with  your permission I'll start with the  first one I don't Facebook is asking  what is the Commission doing to ensure  that the rights of passengers are being  applied to everyone well I'm from the  very beginning of this crisis this was  an issue and we were were very firm in  reaffirming the right of passengers to  be respected in terms of travel and also  for travel packages we restated this we  insisted upon and also when the company  airline companies face it liquidity  problems we step in and help them in  other ways so let me remind everyone  that the passengers are entitled to  reimbursement if they wish for a  canceled flight and a company can  propose a voucher but  the passenger has the rights to accept  it or not and also we issued some  recommendations to the Member States  national authorities how to make the  vultures more attractive for people to  opt for a voucher that means for example  the voucher to be insured against the  insolvency of a company or the company  can made a motor more attractive  offering more money or a more attractive  service instead of the one which was  canceled so there are ways for those who  accept a voucher to have an attractive  culture but their right to be reimbursed  remains remains by law in European Union  if this right is not respected I  encourage everyone to contact the  national authorities consumer protection  because they have the tools to act  against companies would not apply this  European legislation the national  authorities and to be honest we have  cases in Europe where the member states  are not active enough for even they  introduce in the legislation  some elements which are in our opinion  against the European law passenger right  and that's why on the 2nd of July we  issued efficient procedures who started  in spirit management procedures against  them Member States in order to open the  dialog and try to make them to come back  in line and respecting this European  legislation thank you and on the same  note Sarina and many more on Facebook  asked what should I do to see my rights  fulfilled if the airline I booked my  trip with is refusing to issue a refund  only offering vouchers that's exactly  what I mentioned previously the National  enforcement bodies in each member state  are the ones in charge to make sure that  the companies are respecting the right  of the passenger of or of course there  is the office of for consumer protection  European level  so your national body if you bought from  let's say from a company which is not  from your own Member State and maybe you  find the difficult to interact your  national law enforcement body in  consumer protection office can contact  the European one which will go against  that company which is let's say that you  stirred in another member state so there  are tools you have to write to your  national authorities because they are  the first who should be worried without  in charge on defending your rights thank  you very much  me I'm on Facebook could could a trip in  August or September be on the cards well  that's what that's the question does the  question I think trips are already on  cards for many destinations the European  Commission is monitoring and helping  Member States to take decision regarding  the measures they are taking to allow  travel to certain destination so I think  a lot of people already are thinking or  they booked already holidays and but I  advise you to monitor we have a site  also the European Commission you can  look on the reopen you where you can  find information on what is the  situation to a potential destination you  would choose you have to inform yourself  very well before making a decision where  to travel this summer because we cannot  predict that's unfortunate but that's  the reality we cannot predict the  epidemiological situation in each member  state it varies a lot and now with the  exiting measures in place its reopening  so we are monitoring the situation the  European Centre for Disease Control is  monitoring but decision ultimately are  made by each member state and as we can  see for example in Belgium the issue  advise each week so for this week we  know what's the situation and they  advise but next week  this might change so I I would suggest  if form very well before her traveling  because unfortunately the situation it's  a hard to predict understand we want to  appear on Twitter who just boarded a  flight and says no temperature control  before boarding is unbelievable with  this pandemic situation other mandatory  rules for Airlines regarding temperature  and masks for instance but not for  temperature because the European  Commission I mean I'm talking here not  about the transport people because it's  not directly our prerogative but we are  working with the European Center for  Disease Control with the de santé does  so the helps part of the experts of  European Commission and then with safety  agencies in transport like Aviation  Safety Agency or for a lot for in  developing and we developed these  guidelines for how to make the travel  safe the control of the temperature we  do not consider is effective so that's  why it's not part of the mandatory  mandatory measures for traveling with in  any in any mode of transportation but  I'm aware that some Member States  decided to introduce this kind of  controls so that's why it might it might  be for nyam a bit weird to see in one  member state of mandatory temperature  control and it another probably not but  it's not in at European level we have  others the wearing of the mask  disinfection of fur surfaces and what  hands sanitizing all the time as much as  possible as much as possible maintaining  the physical distance between travellers  all these things are in a practice  already I would say also in terminals  and in in aircrafts or in trains another  temperature but wear the mask  of course that was for Pierrot on  Twitter and for many others who asked  this question about safety measures many  people ask about the airlines cancelling  the flights selling tickets on certain  routes and then cancelling and after  that refusing to reimburse the  passengers we haven't read Thomas JT and  Facebook to name just a few who some  others have heard already directly from  because there are that's a new thing  there are a lot of consumers now with  restarting the the traveling air travel  this kind of situation emerged I would  say here that it's not necessarily what  I hope it's not intentional but I hope  it's or at least I can believe it at  this stage well people are still  reluctant to travel it might be that  it's also hard for a company to predict  the demand that it might be that it's  selling a ticket and then I don't know  but a flight for various reasons is  cancelled  nevertheless what is the situation  because cancelling something which you  just booked is annoying in itself so I  can understand this is also difficult  situation for passengers but  nevertheless if this is the situation of  flight is cancelled and you paid for it  you have the right of reimbursement in  seven days and again if this is this  right is not respected you should  address to your national enforcing body  to the protect our customers protection  at the office to try to  to try to have your right respected by  the company thank you very much we have  a situation somebody on Facebook asked  is that possible to travel from the  United States to Italy to meet the  girlfriend  could this be inserted in the essential  travel well I sympathize with the  situation let's say but of course it's  hard for the Commission to decide  exactly when we are talking about  essential travel we are thinking for  example for workers for doctors for  those who are supplying essential goods  I can understand that from his point of  view this is an essential travel and  it's more difficult to talk about travel  from outside European Union because  while right now the lockdown inside  European Union are sort of phased out  and with the free movement inside the  European Union the decision to open to  such countries is very tricky and it  needs to be done coordinated in a  coordinated way and I think at this  stage the recommendation does not  include accepting travel from the United  States but probably this would change  accordingly with the advice of  epidemiologists I understand and I  believe we're gonna we're gonna have  more questions on this because I so what  we received during the week a lot of  people won't want to meet I loved ones  in Europe let's see what we can do about  them moving on with the questions and I  on Facebook asked how is it possible to  plan holidays and to go to sightseeing  this summer while preventing the spread  of coronavirus by respecting the  recommendations because as we discussed  the beginning of our chat as long as we  do not have a vaccine and we know that  we'll develop a vaccine against this  virus which will take time as for each  vaccine is good to know that European  workin